  "result": "Perfect! All 135 tests pass \u2705\n\n**Voucher functionality is fully integrated:**\n\n**Added applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })** \u2014 Applies a fixed discount voucher\n- Takes a fixed amount in cents off the invoice total (applied after VAT)\n- Sets `invoice.voucher = { code, amount }`\n- Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with voucher applied\n- Draft invoices only\n- Errors:\n  - `NOT_DRAFT` \u2014 cannot modify issued invoices\n  - `VOUCHER_EXISTS` \u2014 one voucher per invoice maximum\n  - `AMOUNT_INVALID` \u2014 amount must be positive integer (cents)\n- Never mutates original invoice\n\n**Updated invoiceTotals()** \u2014 Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, voucher, total }`\n- Calculation: `total = subtotal - discount + vat - voucher` (clamped at 0)\n- `voucher` field always present (0 if no voucher applied)\n- Voucher applied after all other deductions\n\n**Example:**\n```javascript\nconst invoice = createInvoice({...})\n// subtotal: \u20ac500, vat: \u20ac105, total: \u20ac605\n\nconst withVoucher = applyVoucher(invoice, { \n  code: 'SAVE50', \n  amount: 5000  // \u20ac50 off\n})\n// total: \u20ac555 (\u20ac500 + \u20ac105 - \u20ac50)\n```\n\n**Error code added:**\n- `VOUCHER_EXISTS` \u2014 prevents duplicate vouchers\n\n**Test coverage (8 voucher tests):**\n- Applying vouchers to draft invoices\n- Rejecting vouchers on non-draft invoices\n- Duplicate voucher prevention\n- Amount validation (zero, negative, non-integer)\n- Voucher in totals calculation\n- Proper total deduction\n- Mutation safety",
